# What must not enter the build context.
#
# `docker/ace-candidate/Dockerfile` does `COPY . /opt/hyperspectrum-sdk`, and
# ACE's equivalent installs a `git archive` of one commit — tracked files and
# nothing else. Everything listed here is what stands between those two being
# the same tree: a local virtualenv, a stale build output, someone's run
# directory, and the caches that follow a developer around.
#
# `.git` in particular: it is large, it is not part of any installed artifact,
# and a build service that clones and builds would otherwise ship the whole
# history into a layer.

.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.worktrees/
.venv/
runs/
dist/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
